{
  "$comment": "Single source of every scoring number (brief Section 4, PLAN Phase 6). Read by src/lib/score/weights.ts (validated with zod) and rendered on /methodology and in docs/METHODOLOGY.md Section 7. Points are risk points: every value is >= 0, so removing a signal can never raise a score (missing data never increases the score). Protective kinds (a report, a manual, a warranty …) carry 0 points: they are listed with their receipt and count as data for confidence, and they are the alternative to the risk kind that would otherwise appear (report_found vs no_report_found, repair findings vs no_repair_info_found).",
  "version": 2,
  "axes": {
    "claims": 0.25,
    "evidence": 0.25,
    "track": 0.3,
    "repair": 0.2
  },
  "points": {
